.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH bap-setup 1  "bap-setup " 
.SH NAME
bap\-setup \- Configure this machine: completions and man pages
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbap\-setup\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-zshrc\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configure this machine: completions and man pages
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be written without writing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-zshrc\fR
Also append an fpath snippet to ~/.zshrc for zsh completions
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print machine\-readable JSON
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  bap setup               # write completions + man pages, print PATH advice
  bap setup \-\-dry\-run     # show what would change
